/P 75 0 R
/E (It was strange, she thought, that the chamomile had been there the whole time. Right there in the corner bed. While she had been bleeding and walking to the kitchen and sitting on the stool, the chamomile had been here, growing, standing patient in the late afternoon sun. It had not known her name. It had not needed to. It had been ready for her for as long as it had been here, which was probably a long time.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
